# Catalog query packages

Follow the project skill `.agents/skills/add-catalog-query/SKILL.md`.

- One folder per domain: `core/database/<domain>/` (see `users/`). Functions take `*database.Catalog` and `DB()`.
- Do not add per-table files to `core/database/` or methods on `Catalog`. Domain errors stay in the table package, except a pure value type's `ErrInvalid`, which lives in its pure `core/<singular>` package (`core/datevalue`, `core/namevalue`, `core/depictionvalue`).
- DDL still goes through catalog migrations, not query packages. The same PR registers the table and its FKs in `catalogmodel` — `.agents/skills/add-catalog-model/SKILL.md`.
- Official resource / vocab `Delete` goes through `deleteimpact` — see `.agents/skills/add-catalog-delete/SKILL.md` and `.cursor/rules/catalog-deletes.mdc`.
- Researcher callers obtain `*database.Catalog` from `catalogsession.Do` / FFI `withProjectCatalog`, not open-per-call. See `.agents/skills/use-catalog-session/SKILL.md`.
- An open-catalog read of the canonical graph follows a `hops.Hop` with `graphcache.Graph.Follow`; a summary composer reads other handles through its `graphcache.InputScope` (`Node`, `Follow`) so its inputs are recorded, and a raw query in a composer reads no other handle. Do not hand-write the association join in SQL; the bridge shape lives in the connectrules registry.
- A walk that must see rows the cache has not loaded, including inside a write, reads SQL in its own package, as `searchindex`'s input lookups do. A write finds the summary rows it moved in `catalog_search_inputs` (`searchindex.ReprojectChanged`). One Evidence graph is walked in memory with `graphcache.Graph.WalkEvidenceGraph` on its loaded `EvidenceGraph`.
- A derived cache registers a typed handle (`graphcache.RegisterKeyed[T]` or `RegisterWhole[T]`) from `init()`, reads only through its `Get`, `GetMany` or `Peek` (each counts as a use; a Check reads none of them), declares its Apply, `DerivedFrom`, lifetime, Check and Cap, adds its row to `docs/catalog-caches.md`, adds its fill to `BenchmarkCacheSizes`, and blank-imports its package in `core/catalogsession/cache_doc_test.go`; never add a field on `Graph` for one.
